<title>UK: U.S. stocks in London static due to Wall St holiday.</title>
<headline>U.S. stocks in London static due to Wall St holiday.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. shares were at a virtual standstill on Monday in Europe due to the closure of Wall Street today for the President's Day public holiday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Dow industrials average closed 33.48 points lower at 6,988.96 on Friday amid broad profit-taking after hitting record levels last week.</p>
<p>The U.S. share market resumes normal trading hours on Tuesday, February 18.</p>
<p>-- Dale Faulken, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
